  "title": "Prompting the Dead (Talqeen)",
  "data": "Besides prompting the dying person, it is recommended to prompt the dead on two occasions:\n(1) When the body is placed in the grave. In this case, it is better for the prompter to grasp the right shoulder of the dead with his right hand and the left shoulder with his left hand, then move the body and say the words of the prompting.\n(2) After the burial. The nearest relative of the dead person should sit at the head of the grave after everyone else has left, and prompt the dead in a loud voice. It is better to put both palms on the grave and bring the mouth close to it. There is no objection, however, if the nearest relative deputes someone else to prompt the dead.\nAccording to reported traditions, when a dead person is prompted with these words, Munkar and Nakir (the two angels who question the dead in their graves) say, “This dead person has been prompted; there is no need to question him. Let us leave.” And they leave without questioning him.\n'Allamah al-Majlisi, may Allah have mercy on him, says: The all-comprehensive form of prompting the dead is as follows:\nاِسْمَعْ اِفْهَمْ يَا فُلَانَ بْنَ فُلَانٍ\nISMA' IFHAM YAA FULAANABNA FULAAN\nListen and understand, O so-and-so, son of so-and-so!\nهَلْ اَنْتَ عَلَى الْعَهْدِ الَّذِىْ فَارَقْتَنَا عَلَيْهِ مِنْ شَهَادَةِ اَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nHAL ANTA A'LAL A'HDIL LADHEE FAARAQTANAA A'LAYHI MIN SHAHAADATI AL LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nAre you upon the covenant upon which you parted from us: the testimony that there is no god but Allah, One, having no partner;\nوَاَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ وَسَيِّدُ النَّبِيِّيْنَ وَخَاتَمُ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ\nWA ANNA MUHAMMADAN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUHOO WA SAYYIDUN NABIYYEENA WA KHAATAMUL MURSALEEN\nthat Muhammad, may Allah bless him and his Household, is His servant and His Messenger, the master of the prophets and the seal of the messengers;\nوَاَنَّ عَلِيًّا اَمِيْرُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَسَيِّدُ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ وَاِمَامٌ افْتَرَضَ اللّٰهُ طَاعَتَهٗ عَلَى الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWA ANNA A'LIYYAN AMEERUL MU'MINEENA WA SAYYIDUL WASIYYEENA WA IMAAMUNIF TARADALLAAHU TAA'ATAHOO A'LAL A'ALAMEEN\nthat Ali is the Commander of the Faithful, the master of the successors, and an Imam whom Allah has made it obligatory upon all the worlds to obey;\nوَاَنَّ الْحَسَنَ وَالْحُسَيْنَ وَعَلِىَّ بْنَ الْحُسَيْنِ وَمُحَمَّدَ بْنَ عَلِىٍّ وَجَعْفَرَ بْنَ مُحَمَّدٍ وَمُوْسَى بْنَ جَعْفَرٍ\nWA ANNAL HASANA WAL HUSAYNA WA A'LIYYABNAL HUSAYNI WA MUHAMMADABNA A'LIYYIN WA JA'FARABNA MUHAMMADIN WA MOOSABNA JA'FAR\nthat al-Hasan, al-Husayn, Ali ibn al-Husayn, Muhammad ibn Ali, Ja'far ibn Muhammad, Musa ibn Ja'far,\nوَعَلِىَّ بْنَ مُوْسٰى وَمُحَمَّدَ بْنَ عَلِىٍّ وَعَلِىَّ بْنَ مُحَمَّدٍ وَالْحَسَنَ بْنَ عَلِىٍّ وَالْقَاۤئِمَ الْحُجَّةَ الْمَهْدِىَّ صَلَوَاتُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِمْ\nWA A'LIYYABNA MOOSAA WA MUHAMMADABNA A'LIYYIN WA A'LIYYABNA MUHAMMADIN WAL HASANABNA A'LIYYIN WAL QAA'IMAL HUJJATAL MAHDIYYA SALAWAATULLAAHI A'LAYHIM\nAli ibn Musa, Muhammad ibn Ali, Ali ibn Muhammad, al-Hasan ibn Ali, and al-Qa'im, the Proof, al-Mahdi, Allah's blessings be upon them,\nاَئِمَّةُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَحُجَجُ اللّٰهِ عَلَى الْخَلْقِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ وَاَئِمَّتَكَ اَئِمَّةُ هُدًى اَبْرَارٌ\nA'IMMATUL MU'MINEENA WA HUJAJULLAAHI A'LAL KHALQI AJMA'EENA WA A'IMMATAKA A'IMMATU HUDAN ABRAAR\nare the Imams of the faithful and the proofs of Allah over all creation; and that your Imams are righteous Imams of guidance?\nيَا فُلَانَ بْنَ فُلَانٍ اِذَا اَتَاكَ الْمَلَكَانِ الْمُقَرَّبَانِ رَسُوْلَيْنِ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالٰى\nYAA FULAANABNA FULAANIN IDHAA ATAAKAL MALAKAANIL MUQARRABAANI RASOOLAYNI MIN I'NDILLAAHI TABAARAKA WA TA'AALAA\nO so-and-so, son of so-and-so, when the two angels drawn near (to Allah) come to you as messengers from Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He,\nوَسَئَلَاكَ عَنْ رَبِّكَ وَعَنْ نَبِيِّكَ وَعَنْ دِيْنِكَ وَعَنْ كِتَابِكَ وَعَنْ قِبْلَتِكَ وَعَنْ اَئِمَّتِكَ\nWA SA'ALAAKA A'N RABBIKA WA A'N NABIYYIKA WA A'N DEENIKA WA A'N KITAABIKA WA A'N QIBLATIKA WA A'N A'IMMATIK\nand ask you about your Lord, your Prophet, your religion, your Book, your qiblah and your Imams,\nفَلَا تَخَفْ وَقُلْ فِىْ جَوَابِهِمَا\nFALAA TAKHAF WA QUL FEE JAWAABIHIMAA\ndo not fear, but say in answer to them:\nاَللّٰهُ جَلَّ جَلَالُهٗ رَبِّىْ وَمُحَمَّدٌ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ نَبِيِّىْ وَالْاِسْلَامُ دِيْنِىْ وَالْقُرْاٰنُ كِتَابِىْ وَالْكَعْبَةُ قِبْلَتِىْ\nALLAAHU JALLA JALAALUHOO RABBEE WA MUHAMMADUN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE NABIYYEE WAL ISLAAMU DEENEE WAL QUR'AANU KITAABEE WAL KA'BATU QIBLATEE\nAllah, majestic is His majesty, is my Lord; Muhammad, may Allah bless him and his Household, is my Prophet; Islam is my religion; the Qur'an is my Book; the Ka'bah is my qiblah;\nوَاَمِيْرُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ عَلِىُّ بْنُ اَبِىْ طَالِبٍ اِمَامِىْ وَالْحَسَنُ بْنُ عَلِىٍّ الْمُجْتَبٰى اِمَامِىْ وَالْحُسَيْنُ بْنُ عَلِىٍّ الشَّهِيْدُ بِكَرْبَلَاۤءَ اِمَامِىْ\nWA AMEERUL MU'MINEENA A'LIYYUBNU ABEE TAALIBIN IMAAMEE WAL HASANUBNU A'LIYYINIL MUJTABAA IMAAMEE WAL HUSAYNUBNU A'LIYYINISH SHAHEEDU BIKARBALAA'A IMAAMEE\nthe Commander of the Faithful, Ali ibn Abi Talib, is my Imam; al-Hasan ibn Ali, the Chosen, is my Imam; al-Husayn ibn Ali, the martyr of Karbala, is my Imam;\nوَعَلِىٌّ زَيْنُ الْعَابِدِيْنَ اِمَامِىْ وَمُحَمَّدٌ بَاقِرُ عِلْمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ اِمَامِىْ وَجَعْفَرٌ الصَّادِقُ اِمَامِىْ وَمُوْسَى الْكَاظِمُ اِمَامِىْ\nWA A'LIYYUN ZAYNUL A'ABIDEENA IMAAMEE WA MUHAMMADUN BAAQIRU I'LMIN NABIYYEENA IMAAMEE WA JA'FARUNIS SAADIQU IMAAMEE WA MOOSAL KAAZIMU IMAAMEE\nAli Zayn al-Abidin is my Imam; Muhammad, who laid open the knowledge of the prophets, is my Imam; Ja'far al-Sadiq is my Imam; Musa al-Kazim is my Imam;\nوَعَلِىٌّ الرِّضَا اِمَامِىْ وَمُحَمَّدٌ الْجَوَادُ اِمَامِىْ وَعَلِىٌّ الْهَادِىْ اِمَامِىْ وَالْحَسَنُ الْعَسْكَرِىُّ اِمَامِىْ وَالْحُجَّةُ الْمُنْتَظَرُ اِمَامِىْ\nWA A'LIYYUNIR RIDAA IMAAMEE WA MUHAMMADUNIL JAWAADU IMAAMEE WA A'LIYYUNIL HAADEE IMAAMEE WAL HASANUL A'SKARIYYU IMAAMEE WAL HUJJATUL MUNTAZARU IMAAMEE\nAli al-Reza is my Imam; Muhammad al-Jawad is my Imam; Ali al-Hadi is my Imam; al-Hasan al-Askari is my Imam; and the Awaited Proof is my Imam.\nهٰؤُلَاۤءِ صَلَوَاتُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ اَئِمَّتِىْ وَسَادَتِىْ وَقَادَتِىْ وَشُفَعَاۤئِىْ\nHAA'ULAA'I SALAWAATULLAAHI A'LAYHIM AJMA'EENA A'IMMATEE WA SAADATEE WA QAADATEE WA SHUFA'AA'EE\nThese, Allah's blessings be upon them all, are my Imams, my masters, my leaders and my intercessors;\nبِهِمْ اَتَوَلّٰى وَمِنْ اَعْدَاۤئِهِمْ اَتَبَرَّاُ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nBIHIM ATAWALLAA WA MIN A'DAA'IHIM ATABARRA'U FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nthem I take as my guardians, and from their enemies I dissociate myself, in this world and the Hereafter.\nثُمَّ اعْلَمْ يَا فُلَانَ بْنَ فُلَانٍ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالٰى نِعْمَ الرَّبُّ وَاَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ نِعْمَ الرَّسُوْلُ\nTHUMMA'LAM YAA FULAANABNA FULAANIN ANNALLAAHA TABAARAKA WA TA'AALAA NI'MAR RABBU WA ANNA MUHAMMADAN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE NI'MAR RASOOL\nThen know, O so-and-so, son of so-and-so, that Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, is the best Lord; that Muhammad, may Allah bless him and his Household, is the best Messenger;\nوَاَنَّ اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ عَلِىَّ بْنَ اَبِىْ طَالِبٍ وَاَوْلَادَهُ الْاَئِمَّةَ الْاَحَدَ عَشَرَ نِعْمَ الْاَئِمَّةُ\nWA ANNA AMEERAL MU'MINEENA A'LIYYABNA ABEE TAALIBIN WA AWLAADAHUL A'IMMATAL AHADA A'SHARA NI'MAL A'IMMAH\nthat the Commander of the Faithful, Ali ibn Abi Talib, and his descendants, the eleven Imams, are the best Imams;\nوَاَنَّ مَا جَاۤءَ بِهٖ مُحَمَّدٌ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ حَقٌّ وَاَنَّ الْمَوْتَ حَقٌّ وَسُؤَالَ مُنْكَرٍ وَنَكِيْرٍ فِى الْقَبْرِ حَقٌّ\nWA ANNA MAA JAA'A BIHEE MUHAMMADUN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE HAQQUN WA ANNAL MAWTA HAQQUN WA SU'AALA MUNKARIN WA NAKEERIN FIL QABRI HAQQ\nthat what Muhammad, may Allah bless him and his Household, brought is true; that death is true; that the questioning of Munkar and Nakir in the grave is true;\nوَالْبَعْثَ حَقٌّ وَالنُّشُوْرَ حَقٌّ وَالصِّرَاطَ حَقٌّ وَالْمِيْزَانَ حَقٌّ وَتَطَايُرَ الْكُتُبِ حَقٌّ وَالْجَنَّةَ حَقٌّ وَالنَّارَ حَقٌّ\nWAL BA'THA HAQQUN WAN NUSHOORA HAQQUN WAS SIRAATA HAQQUN WAL MEEZAANA HAQQUN WA TATAAYURAL KUTUBI HAQQUN WAL JANNATA HAQQUN WAN NAARA HAQQ\nthat the resurrection is true, the raising up is true, the Bridge is true, the Scale is true, the flying of the records of deeds is true, Paradise is true, and the Fire is true;\nوَاَنَّ السَّاعَةَ اٰتِيَةٌ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَبْعَثُ مَنْ فِى الْقُبُوْرِ\nWA ANNAS SAA'ATA AATIYATUN LAA RAYBA FEEHAA WA ANNALLAAHA YAB'ATHU MAN FIL QUBOOR\nand that the Hour will come, there is no doubt about it, and that Allah will raise up those who are in the graves.\nThen the prompter should ask:\nاَفَهِمْتَ يَا فُلَانُ\nAFAHIMTA YAA FULAAN\nHave you understood, O so-and-so?\nAccording to a reported tradition, when a dead person is addressed with these words, he answers, “Yes, I understand.”\nThe prompter should then say:\nثَبَّتَكَ اللّٰهُ بِالْقَوْلِ الثَّابِتِ هَدَاكَ اللّٰهُ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ\nTHABBATAKALLAAHU BIL QAWLITH THAABITI HADAAKALLAAHU ILAA SIRAATIM MUSTAQEEM\nMay Allah make you firm with the firm word! May Allah guide you to a straight path!\nعَرَّفَ اللّٰهُ بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَ اَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ فِىْ مُسْتَقَرٍّ مِنْ رَّحْمَتِهٖ\nA'RRAFALLAAHU BAYNAKA WA BAYNA AWLIYAA'IKA FEE MUSTAQARRIN MIR RAHMATIH\nMay Allah bring you and your guardians to know one another in a resting place of His mercy!\nHe may then add:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ جَافِ الْاَرْضَ عَنْ جَنْبَيْهِ وَاصْعَدْ بِرُوْحِهٖ اِلَيْكَ وَلَقِّهٖ مِنْكَ بُرْهَانًا اَللّٰهُمَّ عَفْوَكَ عَفْوَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA JAAFIL ARDA A'N JANBAYHI WAS'AD BIROOHIHEE ILAYKA WA LAQQIHEE MINKA BURHAANAN ALLAAHUMMA A'FWAKA A'FWAK\nO Allah, keep the earth away from his sides, raise his soul up to You, and grant him a proof from You. O Allah, (we beg) Your pardon, Your pardon!\nWith these words Shaykh Abbas al-Qummi closes his book al-Baqiyat al-Salihat, writing: “Deliberately, I have chosen the word ‘pardon’ to be the closing word of this book of mine, hoping trustfully that my Lord will include me, and all those who benefit from this book, among those whom He pardons, since sins have blackened my face.\n“The last of this book was written on the last Friday (the 19th) of the sacred month of Muharram, AH 1345, in the vicinity of our Imam and master, the poisoned, the estranged and the oppressed, Abu'l-Hasan Ali ibn Musa al-Reza, may the peace of the Ever-living, Self-subsisting Lord be upon him and upon his forefathers.\n“First and last, all praise be to Allah, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his Household. 'Abbas Muhammad Rida al-Qummi.”"
}
